	•	The Connection: The Shard exists outside of linear time. Touching it connects a person to the "Timelessness" of the Colliders.
	•	The Acoustic Loop:
	•	Eleni (1901) hears James (1982) and Future Elena (1986).
	•	James (1982) hears Eleni (1901) and Future Elena (1986).
	•	Elena (1986) hears James and Eleni, and shouts the warning that echoes back to the past.
	•	The Isolation: Only those who have touched the Shard can hear these echoes. To bystanders (like Liz and Mikey), the Shard-bearer appears to be talking to themselves or hallucinating.




Here is a detailed synopsis of The Ancient Era of the Colliders saga, focusing primarily on The Book of Lucius.
This synopsis synthesizes the narrative arcs of Lucius, Marcus, and the young Mark Antony, integrating the specific historical details, the quantum mechanics of the "Mirror Moment," and the catastrophic birth of the Shard.

The Colliders Saga – The Ancient Era: The Book of Lucius
Logline
In 67 BCE, a pacifist Roman scholar is tasked with retrieving a mysterious Greek celestial computer and a volatile urn of "star dust." His journey home culminates in a quantum cataclysm at sea—a lightning strike that birthing a Golden Orb, sinking his ship, and splitting reality into two diverging timelines based on the split-second decision of a young Mark Antony.

Part I: The Scholar and the Wolf (Rome)
The Black Sheep Lucius Fabius (21) is a brilliant but isolated scholar in a Rome obsessed with conquest. While his father and older brother, Marcus (24), worship Mars, Lucius worships geometry and astronomy. He is deeply uncomfortable with slavery and the brutality of the Colosseum. He views the stars not as gods, but as a clockwork mechanism waiting to be understood.
The Crucible of Cruelty To "toughen him up," his father forces him to attend the games. There, amidst the gore, Lucius meets Marcus Antonius (Mark Antony), a precocious, arrogant, yet magnetic 16-year-old apprentice soldier under his brother's command. While Mark is captivated by the violence, Lucius is repulsed. He flees the arena, vowing to pursue knowledge over carnage.
The Bridge Between Worlds Lucius attempts to connect with his brother Marcus by explaining how celestial mechanics (the position of the sun and moon) can be weaponized for tactical advantage on the battlefield. Marcus, usually dismissive, is impressed by the practical application of Lucius's "useless" studies. This earns Lucius a fragile respect and sets the stage for his mission.

Part II: The Mechanism and the Mystery (Rhodes)
The Summons Marcus, stationed in the East during the Mithridatic Wars, sends a crimson-sealed letter to Rome. He has acquired two items of immense power:
	1	The Antikythera Mechanism: A complex bronze computer of gears and dials found in a market in Nisibis.
	2	The Monazite Urn: A heavy, sealed clay vessel containing "Celestial Aether" (radioactive thorium/monazite dust), rumored to be the power source or catalyst for the mechanism. Marcus fears his superstitious soldiers will destroy these "pagan" objects. He implores Lucius to come to Rhodes to retrieve and safeguard them.
The Journey East Lucius travels to Rhodes, accompanied by young Mark Antony, who acts as his protector. During the voyage, they spot a jagged, crocodile-shaped rocky outcrop (Scopulus) near the island of Aegilia—a landmark they jokingly memorize, unaware it will soon become their purgatory.
The Ritual In Rhodes, the brothers reunite. Before departing, Marcus introduces Lucius to a Mithraic ritual involving kykeon (a hallucinogen). Lucius experiences terrifying visions of an "Underwater Star" and a massive sea monster (Ketos). He realizes the Mechanism is not just a calculator, but a key to understanding the structure of reality itself.

Part III: The Quantum Cataclysm (The Return Voyage)
The Cargo Lucius, Mark, and a small crew board the merchant ship The Aurelia (or Sea Serpent) for the return to Rome. The Antikythera Mechanism and the heavy Monazite Urn are lashed to the mast.
The Mirror Moment (The Bifurcation) As the ship prepares to depart, a pivotal quantum event occurs involving Mark Antony. He stands before a polished bronze mirror, adjusting his medallion. He experiences a profound sense of déjà vu.
	•	The Split: In this nanosecond, Mark's choice—whether to touch the mirror or push it away—interacting with the latent energy of the nearby Monazite Urn, causes reality to split into two distinct, parallel timelines (Universe A and Universe B).
The Storm and the Golden Orb A violent storm strikes near Antikythera. A bolt of hyper-intense lightning (the "Zeus-Electron") strikes the mast, grounding itself directly through the Monazite Urn.
	•	The Reaction: The electrical discharge triggers a localized nuclear transmutation within the urn. The urn disintegrates, birthing a Golden Orb of superheated plasma and quantum-entangled matter.
	•	The Descent: The Orb, defying gravity and physics, burns a hole through the deck. It melts its way down through the ship, glowing with a terrifying brilliance.
The Divergence of Fate
	•	In Universe A (Our History): The Orb’s path ignites a catastrophic fire. The ship is consumed. The Antikythera Mechanism sinks but is relatively intact (later to be found corroded). The Orb melts through the hull and hits the water, cooling instantly into the Obsidian Shard—a quantum-entangled artifact that settles into a brain coral on the seafloor.
	•	In Universe B (The Alternate): The Orb’s path is slightly different. The fire is contained. The ship limps back to port. The Mechanism is saved and studied, leading to a technologically advanced Roman Empire.

Part IV: Marooned (Universe A)
The Sinking In our timeline, The Aurelia is doomed. Lucius and Mark are thrown into the churning Aegean. Amidst the drowning crew and debris, they remember the "Crocodile" rock (Scopulus) they spotted on the outward journey. Fighting the current and sharks, they swim for their lives.
Survival on Scopulus They wash up on the barren, sharp rocks of Scopulus. For days, the scholar and the apprentice soldier are stripped of their status. They survive on limpets, dew collected in hollows, and sheer will.
	•	The Bond: The experience transforms them. Lucius learns resilience; Mark learns humility and the value of intellect. They bond over the trauma of the "Golden Orb" they saw burning beneath the waves even after the ship sank.
The Rescue Mark manages to light a signal fire using a saved flint kit. A Cretan fishing boat rescues them. They return to civilization changed men. Lucius is haunted by the loss of the Mechanism and the creation of the Shard (though he doesn't know what it is). Mark Antony begins his ascent to power, hardened by the ordeal.

Key Narrative Elements & Mechanics
	•	The Shard's Genesis: The Shard is not the Antikythera Mechanism. It is the remnant of the Monazite Urn that was transmuted by the lightning strike. It contains a "particle-soul" entangled with its twin in Universe B.
	•	The Colliders: At the moment of the Shard's creation (the lightning strike), the Colliders (beings from a universe destroyed by this event) attach themselves ethereally to the Shard in Universe A. They exist as a silent, non-corporeal resonance around the Shard for 2,000 years until 1983.
	•	Audio Footprints: Lucius and Mark become the first "Shard-Bearers." By being near the Golden Orb/Shard during its birth, they leave permanent "audio footprints." Future bearers (like Eleni or James) might hear Lucius's screams or Mark's commands echoing in "Echo Zones" near the sea.
The Legacy
The Ancient Era ends with the Shard resting in the coral reef near Antikythera, humming with the silent presence of the Colliders, waiting for the sponge diver Eleni to touch it in 1901. The Antikythera Mechanism lies nearby, a broken key to a door that was blown off its hinges.



Here is a detailed synopsis of The Awakening Era of the Colliders saga, focusing on the events of December 1982, the creation of the Sentinels, and the pivotal first moments of the rogue AI, Sato XI (STXI).
