The Breath Before Time The narrative begins in a state of absolute, perfect stillness. There is no space, no time, only the Electron existing as a singularity—everywhere and nowhere at once. It possesses a consciousness defined not by thought, but by being. It is the "Reason" pondering its own existence.
The Wobble In a moment of quantum indecision—a desire to know "What is the reason for Reason?"—the Electron trembles. This infinitesimal "Wobble" breaks the symmetry of nothingness.
