Below is a definitive plan for structuring your MVP DAW-style application in vanilla JavaScript using ES modules. Each module is described with:
	1.	Context Statement – A statement explaining the module’s role within the application.
	2.	Dependencies – Exactly which modules or utility functions it imports (if any).
	3.	Interface – All classes, methods, parameters, and return values that the module exports. No extraneous or optional methods are included; everything listed must be implemented.
	4.	Implementation Notes – Clarifications on how the methods work together.

Use this plan to ensure that each module can be created in isolation by a developer or agent who only needs the module’s context and interface definition to build a fully compatible piece of the application.

9. FileManagement.js

Context Statement

The FileManagement module handles loading audio files from the user’s file system or from a URL, passing decoded AudioBuffer objects to external modules as needed. It also exports and imports project data (JSON).

Dependencies
	•	Imports AudioEngine to decode audio files.
	•	Imports StateManager to retrieve or set the project state.

import { AudioEngine } from './AudioEngine.js';
import { StateManager } from './StateManager.js';

Interface

/**
 * @class FileManagement
 * Handles audio file loading and project import/export.
 */
export class FileManagement {
  /**
   * @param {AudioEngine} audioEngine - Used to decode audio data.
   * @param {StateManager} stateManager - Used to retrieve or store project state.
   */
  constructor(audioEngine, stateManager);

  /**
   * Opens an audio file from a File object and returns its AudioBuffer as a Promise.
   * @param {File} file - A file chosen via <input> or drag-and-drop.
   * @returns {Promise<AudioBuffer>} - Resolves with the decoded AudioBuffer.
   */
  openAudioFile(file);

  /**
   * Loads audio data from a provided URL and returns its AudioBuffer as a Promise.
   * @param {string} url - The URL of the audio file.
   * @returns {Promise<AudioBuffer>} - Resolves with the decoded AudioBuffer.
   */
  loadAudioFromURL(url);

  /**
   * Exports the current project data (tracks, regions, timeline info) in JSON format.
   * @returns {string} - A JSON string representing the entire project state.
   */
  exportProjectData();

  /**
   * Imports previously saved project data from JSON and updates the current state accordingly.
   * @param {string} projectJSON - A JSON string containing saved project state.
   * @returns {void}
   */
  importProjectData(projectJSON);
}

Implementation Notes
	•	openAudioFile() and loadAudioFromURL() both use audioEngine.loadAudioFile() internally to decode the data.
	•	exportProjectData() retrieves data from stateManager.getState() and stringifies it.
	•	importProjectData() calls stateManager.setState() with the parsed JSON.

8. EditingTools.js

Context Statement

The EditingTools module implements non-destructive editing actions: cut, copy, paste, and optional undo/redo. It communicates with the RegionManager to manipulate region data.

Dependencies
	•	Imports RegionManager for region manipulation.
	•	Imports utility functions from utils.js for ID generation or data copying.

import { RegionManager } from './RegionManager.js';
import { generateUniqueId } from './utils.js';

Interface

/**
 * @class EditingTools
 * Provides editing actions on regions such as cut, copy, and paste.
 */
export class EditingTools {
  /**
   * @param {RegionManager} regionManager - Used for direct region manipulation.
   */
  constructor(regionManager);

  /**
   * Cuts a region into two pieces at a specified time. The original region is shortened,
   * and a new region is created for the second half.
   * @param {string} regionId - Unique ID of the region to cut.
   * @param {number} cutTime - Absolute timeline time in seconds where the cut occurs.
   * @returns {string} - The ID of the newly created region after the cut.
   */
  cutRegion(regionId, cutTime);

  /**
   * Copies a region’s data and stores it in a temporary clipboard-like structure for future pasting.
   * @param {string} regionId - Unique ID of the region to copy.
   * @returns {void}
   */
  copyRegion(regionId);

  /**
   * Pastes the most recently copied region to a target track at a specified start time.
   * The newly pasted region receives a new unique ID.
   * @param {string} targetTrackId - The track ID where the pasted region should be placed.
   * @param {number} startTime - The start time for the pasted region on the timeline, in seconds.
   * @returns {string} - The ID of the newly created pasted region.
   */
  pasteRegion(targetTrackId, startTime);
}

Implementation Notes
	•	An internal clipboard variable can store the most recently copied region’s AudioBuffer and duration.
	•	When pasting, the new region uses a fresh ID (via generateUniqueId) but copies the same buffer reference.

6. WaveformRenderer.js

Context Statement

The WaveformRenderer provides functions to generate waveform data from AudioBuffer objects and draw them onto a <canvas> element at the correct zoom level.

Dependencies
	•	Imports utility functions from utils.js for any needed calculations.

import { clamp } from './utils.js';

Interface

/**
 * @class WaveformRenderer
 * Generates and draws waveforms from AudioBuffer data.
 */
export class WaveformRenderer {
  /**
   * Constructor that can establish any internal buffers or settings.
   */
  constructor();

  /**
   * Generates waveform data arrays (peak values) from an AudioBuffer for visual rendering.
   * @param {AudioBuffer} audioBuffer - The source audio data.
   * @param {number} samplesPerPixel - How many audio samples to analyze per pixel.
   * @returns {Float32Array} - An array of peak values suitable for waveform rendering.
   */
  generateWaveformData(audioBuffer, samplesPerPixel);

  /**
   * Draws the waveform to a given 2D canvas context.
   * @param {CanvasRenderingContext2D} ctx - The 2D context of the canvas to draw on.
   * @param {Float32Array} waveformData - Peak values generated by generateWaveformData.
   * @param {number} width - The width of the region’s canvas in pixels.
   * @param {number} height - The height of the region’s canvas in pixels.
   * @returns {void}
   */
  drawWaveform(ctx, waveformData, width, height);
}

Implementation Notes
	•	generateWaveformData is typically called once for each audio file; the data can be cached.
	•	drawWaveform must iterate over waveformData and draw lines or polygons representing the peaks.

7. ZoomController.js

Context Statement

The ZoomController manages horizontal zoom (time scaling) and horizontal scroll offset in the arrangement view. Other modules call its methods to adjust the zoom level and retrieve the current scaling factors.

Dependencies
	•	Imports utility functions from utils.js if needed.

import { clamp } from './utils.js';

Interface

/**
 * @class ZoomController
 * Manages time scaling (zoom) and scrolling for the timeline.
 */
export class ZoomController {
  /**
   * Constructor that initializes the default zoomLevel and offsetX.
   */
  constructor();

  /**
   * Increases the current zoom level by a fixed step, up to a defined maximum.
   * @returns {void}
   */
  zoomIn();

  /**
   * Decreases the current zoom level by a fixed step, down to a defined minimum.
   * @returns {void}
   */
  zoomOut();

  /**
   * Scrolls the timeline viewport to the left by a given number of pixels.
   * @param {number} distance - Pixels to scroll to the left.
   * @returns {void}
   */
  scrollLeft(distance);

  /**
   * Scrolls the timeline viewport to the right by a given number of pixels.
   * @param {number} distance - Pixels to scroll to the right.
   * @returns {void}
   */
  scrollRight(distance);

  /**
   * Retrieves the current zoom level (time-to-pixel ratio).
   * @returns {number} - The current zoom factor.
   */
  getZoomLevel();

  /**
   * Retrieves the current horizontal offset in pixels.
   * @returns {number} - The current scroll offset, in pixels.
   */
  getOffsetX();
}

Implementation Notes
	•	The minimum zoom level could be set to 1.0 and the maximum to some fixed value, e.g., 10.0.
