e stars, for the vastness of the cosmos, and not for the blood-soaked sands of the arena, a place of death and degradation.A single thought, clear and unwavering, crystallized in his mind: He would pursue knowledge, not carnage. He would strive to understand the universe, not conquer it. This horrifying display had forged his resolve, solidifying his path, steering him away from the barbaric brutality of the arena and towards the pursuit of understanding the cosmos, a road that was clear and unwavering in his mind. He vowed that he would not let this place corrupt him, he would not let his father’s values pollute his own mind, that he would find his own way, a path towards knowledge and truth.

