e, a low rumble that resonated with his own inner strength. "But so is the strength to enforce it, don't you agree, Lucius?" he added, his gaze holding Lucius’s own with a deep and penetrating power.Marcus scoffed. "He does not need to teach you that nonsense, Marcelluas, you must focus on your training. Focus on the task at hand, I will not have you distracted with his useless ramblings," he rolled his eyes at Lucius, a clear display of his disdain.Marcelluas looked calmly at Marcus, a sly smile playing on his lips, a knowing look that spoke of a shared secret, before returning his gaze to Lucius. "Perhaps you misunderstand, Marcus. I respect knowledge in all its forms, be it the precise angles of celestial bodies, or the perfect strike of a gladius," he gave Marcus a nod of acknowledgment before returning his gaze back to Lucius, his smile widening. "I hope that you will find that I am not like these others, Lucius. Perhaps you and I could find common ground with both the stars and the sand,” he added, his voice low and soft, yet filled with a subtle challenge, an invitation to understand the complexities that lay hidden beneath his surface.Lucius nodded slowly, intrigued and yet uncertain, unable to quite put his finger on what he was feeling. There was an undeniable magnetism to Marcelluas, a powerful combination of intelligence and charisma that was both compelling and slightly unsettling, a dangerous charm that seemed to both draw him in, whilst setting his teeth on edge. He seemed to embody the Roman ideal of a strong warrior, yet he also harbored a genuine interest in the intellectual pursuits that Lucius held dear, a strange combination that both fascinated and confused him. There was something intriguing in the way his face seemed to express the dualities of both science and combat, a strange balance that seemed almost impossible. He could see in him a kindred spirit, a flicker of intellectual curiosity and perhaps a shared desire to understand the mechanics of the world, not just the mechanics of war, yet, he was wary of the glimpse of something darker lurking behind those keen eyes, a love for the brutality that surrounded them, a love that Lucius could never truly understand. Marcelluas was a puzzle, a complex tapestry of seeming contradictions that left Lucius both captivated and hesitant, both intrigued and wary, a mixture of emotions that he found impossible to reconcile. He was, perhaps, the most dangerous of all of them, a compelling and yet complex figure that might one day pose a great threat.
